# 2025-06-16 12:56:43.400554
+Using this transaction list, create a web application.Create a comprehensive React TypeScript cash flow management web application with the following specifications:
+
+## Core Features Required:
+
+### 1. Transaction Management
+- Import/upload transaction lists (CSV, JSON formats)
+- Manual transaction entry with fields: date, amount, category, description, type (inflow/outflow)
+- Edit and delete existing transactions
+- Categorize transactions (Revenue, Expenses, Operating Costs, etc.)
+
+### 2. Dashboard Components
+Create a modern dashboard with these key widgets:
+
+**Cash Inflows Widget:**
+- Display all positive cash flows
+- Show total inflows for current month, quarter, year
+- Visual chart showing inflow trends over time
+- Category breakdown of income sources
+
+**Cash Outflows Widget:**
+- Display all negative cash flows  
+- Show total outflows for current month, quarter, year
+- Visual chart showing outflow trends over time
+- Category breakdown of expense types
+
+**Cash Runway Widget:**
+- Calculate months of cash remaining based on last 6 months burn rate
+- Display prominent runway indicator with color coding (green >12 months, yellow 6-12 months, red <6 months)
+- Show net cash burn rate per month
+- Historical runway trend chart
+
+**13-Week Cash Forecast Widget:**
+- Generate weekly cash balance projections for next 13 weeks
+- Based on historical income/expense patterns
+- Interactive chart showing projected ending cash balance each week
+- Scenario planning with optimistic/realistic/pessimistic views
+
+### 3. Analytics & Insights
+- Net cash burn calculation and trending
+- Largest spending categories analysis with visual charts
+- Largest income sources analysis
+- Month-over-month cash flow comparison
+- Operational improvement recommendations based on spending patterns
+
+### 4. Technical Requirements
+- React 18+ with TypeScript
+- Modern UI framework (Tailwind CSS or Material-UI)
+- Chart.js or Recharts for data visualization
+- Responsive design for desktop and mobile
+- Local storage for data persistence
+- Export functionality (PDF reports, CSV data)
+
+### 5. File Structure
+Organize as:
+

